":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T00:28:51-07:00","id":531776,"title":"","content":"I've updated the Children of the Thorns with the last two attainments, per a request I received!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T02:44:52-08:00","id":746235,"title":"","content":"Both the standard version of Insomnium and the Magic-based alternative are updated for the Alucinor to conform to the new Dream Form systems, as outlined in Beast. I made sure they have their own little benefit similar to Beasts using their Horrors.<br /> <br /> I may tweak them further as Mage and Changeling hit, as I'm sure both will expand on the system a bit more than Beast's core did (though I do need to finish the Beast core, so let me know if there's something more than the entry on page 99), and as it is it's still shackled to 1e changeling dream rules for actual manipulation (dream intensity, for instance).<br /> <br /> I'm admittedly a bit tired so the wordings might not be that great, feel free to suggest ways to clean the language up (comments are open)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T22:52:57-08:00","id":778819,"title":"","content":"Updated Forbidden Lore's 2nd edition version to account for Beast. Let me know if anyone has any commentary about my handling of Satiety; it sounded like a good idea, but I have no way to test it to see if it works as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T03:56:02-08:00","id":778901,"title":"","content":"Critique on Blood Tenebrus 2.0:<br /> <br /> Essence Shield kinda goes on a completely different direction than the other ranks. 1) Assuming you have both the 4th and 2nd rank active... What happens with the essence-like properties of vitae gained from Ephemeral Hand, coupled with Essence Shield's property of said vitae becoming an &quot;Universal Bane&quot;? 2) What happens if you activate Essence Shield while being willfully ridden by a spirit with Fettered Form? It would start to cook within you. Or maybe it would be a gory way to commit slow, agonizing suicide.<br /> <br /> Basically, drop the Bane property.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T04:47:40-08:00","id":778923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=778901#post778901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Critique on Blood Tenebrus 2.0:<br /> <br /> Essence Shield kinda goes on a completely different direction than the other ranks. 1) Assuming you have both the 4th and 2nd rank active... What happens with the essence-like properties of vitae gained from Ephemeral Hand, coupled with Essence Shield's property of said vitae becoming an &quot;Universal Bane&quot;? 2) What happens if you activate Essence Shield while being willfully ridden by a spirit with Fettered Form? It would start to cook within you. Or maybe it would be a gory way to commit slow, agonizing suicide.<br /> <br /> Basically, drop the Bane property.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) What happens is you have essence in the vitae, but no spirit will want it because the vitae is also a bane. Sort of like if a Loci was surrounded in a given spirit's bane; they'd know there's essence there, but still not want to/be able to touch it. Being a bane doesn't interact with essence directly, though, so you just have two powers active that maybe aren't the most useful combination. But it's not like that can't happen in other disciplines.<br /> 2) That's a good point, but easy enough to fix with a note saying it doesn't affect himself or a spirit called in via the 5th dot. Adding that.<br /> <br /> It does indeed go in a somewhat different direction, but still fits the themes and follows up on altering how the spirit world reacts to him, and to me doesn't seem as disparate as some of the different levels of even the core disciplines, really. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T13:49:43-08:00","id":779233,"title":"","content":"Forbidden Lore is a really, really cool mechanic. Until Promethean 2E comes out, this is probably how I'll model mortal Alchemists. Another thing I thought of reading through this, is that the whole vibe of the writeup is deeply Lovecraftian, and fits within Mummy's wheelhouse to perfection. I don't know if you have the Mummy books or not, but this would fit quite nicely for the cultists of the Arisen. Exposure to a Mummy wears down your sanity in a very Lovecraftian way. Makes sense to me their cultists might pick up Utterances and/or Affinities by exposure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:59:16-08:00","id":779676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=779233#post779233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forbidden Lore is a really, really cool mechanic. Until Promethean 2E comes out, this is probably how I'll model mortal Alchemists. Another thing I thought of reading through this, is that the whole vibe of the writeup is deeply Lovecraftian, and fits within Mummy's wheelhouse to perfection. I don't know if you have the Mummy books or not, but this would fit quite nicely for the cultists of the Arisen. Exposure to a Mummy wears down your sanity in a very Lovecraftian way. Makes sense to me their cultists might pick up Utterances and/or Affinities by exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like it! The thing there is that it's a 2nd edition upgrade of a 1st edition system from Mirrors. Mummy's still 1st edition, so it still fits easily with the 1st edition rules for it, so if you have Mirrors I'd suggest using that. If you're using mummy in a 2nd edition game, I unfortunately don't know enough to help you, past saying the system should work pretty much the same way, I dont think mummies had any special considerations to take into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T01:03:42-08:00","id":793017,"title":"","content":"Small question regarding your <i>Gift of the Void Beyond</i>, are you planning on revisiting it and converting it into 2E mechanics for Shadow Gifts? I'm curious, since I'm tempted to weave it into my stuff as another way for a werewolf to become one of the Weeping Wolves (written by NeoTiamat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T21:13:09-08:00","id":795367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=793017#post793017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small question regarding your <i>Gift of the Void Beyond</i>, are you planning on revisiting it and converting it into 2E mechanics for Shadow Gifts? I'm curious, since I'm tempted to weave it into my stuff as another way for a werewolf to become one of the Weeping Wolves (written by NeoTiamat).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually considering that, one of my thoughts being &quot;Does anyone even care about that bit of homebrew enough to convert it?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, that being said, I'll see about doing so in the next few days, if I have a chance, since it seems like there is indeed interest!<br /> <br /> Will likely need to revisit some of the mechanics, given the difference in how Harmony works and what it represents, for instance, as well as the balance of gifts in general. And Paradox, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 12-30-2015, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T11:26:00-08:00","id":796922,"title":"","content":"Here's my first draft of the aforementioned update, which I'll add to the first post: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Qq4rTwv96anwn9rNd7ZkKWDcL0lEnDo4KerP_LYNAI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I decided to focus more on forsaking (no pun intended) your Renown rather than relying on broken Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T13:33:49-08:00","id":797000,"title":"","content":"What is the point of penalizing the gift use with their renown if you're going to give it a bonus? Pick a side.<br /> <br /> Anomaly's blacklash is generally poor considering someone could have a spontaneous volcanic eruption in the middle of the scene. It virtually trumps every environmental tilt-causing gift.<br /> <br /> Release needs an actual blacklash, probably on top of that caveat.<br /> <br /> Make Havok's blacklash count failures as dramatic and count as exceptional with three successes.<br /> <br /> Aside for those editorial notes, not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T21:59:31-08:00","id":797192,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean on that first part? None of the gifts give any bonus to renown.<br /> <br /> You're probably right about anomaly. I've changed it to limit the tilt's size, too, and added an extra bit of the backlash. Still, the main balancing factor is how obvious it is, and that it innately ties the effect to your character, so it can't be hidden (Thus likely causing you trouble if it's done in the city or other populated areas).<br /> <br /> You're probably right about release too, but I've kept it fairly minor.<br /> <br /> I feel if 1-2 successes still work as successes, it's less of a backlash and becomes almost beneficial, as it's far more likely that any power being activated will have enough dice to make at least a basic success more likely. Thus why I made them also count as dramatic failures, to make it a bit of an 'all or nothing' drawback.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:51:54-08:00","id":797224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=796922#post796922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my first draft of the aforementioned update, which I'll add to the first post: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Qq4rTwv96anwn9rNd7ZkKWDcL0lEnDo4KerP_LYNAI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I decided to focus more on forsaking (no pun intended) your Renown rather than relying on broken Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn. I am liking this version of the Gift of the Void.<br /> XD<br /> <br /> It's a pretty interesting direction you took with the Renown. The more you have of it, the more difficult it is to successfully invoke any of the Facets.<br /> <br /> I wanted to add something, though. Almost all the existing Gifts in Werewolf 2E that I've seen (including the Gift of Cities in the link below) have Facets which grow more effective the more dots you have in a specific type of Renown. Perhaps you can apply that here? Only with [6 - Renown]?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Giver of Gifts: 2 [Werewolf: The Forsaken] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Let me give an example for a possible revision with the Anomaly Facet...<br /> <br /> &quot;The Uratha creates an Environmental Tilt of her choice on the surrounding area (to a limit of about a 100 foot radius multiplied by [6 - Cunning]).&quot;<br /> <br /> Would that work? Or perhaps it might be too powerful to incorporate Renown (or lack of it) more into the mechanics?<br /> <br /> On a related note, this is probably a very good reason for an Uratha - Forsaken or Pure - to invest in a rite which flays off his Renown (perhaps applying a Sanctity Rule for the EXP you had spent on it in the first place).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:57:29-08:00","id":797226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=797000#post797000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point of penalizing the gift use with their renown if you're going to give it a bonus? Pick a side.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think that having a flat +5 dice that's offset by the Renown makes sense. It would certainly give you a reason to flay off your Renown (if that rite from the Pure supplement is converted), and it also opens up hooks where conventional packs could encounter Ghost Wolves who shun the Oath in favor of honoring those 'alien' Void spirits that grant such a dangerous Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T22:28:16-08:00","id":797666,"title":"","content":"I'll take a look at it tomorrow to see about adding some scaling, I hadn't even considered that when I was converting them. Definitely doable since I have some things that are success based that could be anti-renown based instead.<br /> <br /> And oh, yeah, if Ephsy meant it was pointless to give a +5 to the gift activation, the point of that is to create 'anti-renown' as a bonus, still giving you an effective '3 trait' dice pool. So really, you can think of it as (5 - Renown) in parentheses as its own trait, rather than adding 5 and then subtracting renown, if it helps visualize what it's meant to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T10:22:48-08:00","id":797858,"title":"","content":"There we go, I added a few scaling bits to it, tweaking some of the other mechanics to match, let me know what you think. I wasn't able to think of anything for Release, but if anyone has any ideas, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T21:41:23-08:00","id":798099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=797858#post797858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There we go, I added a few scaling bits to it, tweaking some of the other mechanics to match, let me know what you think. I wasn't able to think of anything for Release, but if anyone has any ideas, let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I'm liking a lot of the revisions. Though a few things seem to be muddled up, now.<br /> <br /> For Anomaly, you could probably rephrase the bit on damage rating and/or penalty so that it's easier to understand? I can't really make heads or tails on how to interpret the description.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Uratha creates an Environmental Tilt of her choice on the surrounding area (to a limit of about a 100 foot radius), with a rating, damage, or penalty equal to (5 - Cunning), if appropriate (capped at the normal limit the tilt has, if any, and a minimum of 1). </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> Perhaps, you can retain this as being based on successes. And instead, make the area of effect be what's determined by the werewolf's (lack of) Cunning Renown, Something like &quot;To a limit of a 50-foot radius multiplied by (5 - Cunning), with a minimum of 25 feet at Cunning 5&quot;.<br /> <br /> For Release, maybe in addition to flinging the Condition or Tilt at your opponent, perhaps you can have its duration multiplied by &quot;[5 - Honor]&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-02-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T18:38:37-08:00","id":800002,"title":"","content":"Well not all environmental tilts have a radius, but I can see that working out. Not on my PC at the moment but I'll see about tweaking that later.<br /> <br /> As for release, the problem there is a lot of conditions/tilts have no set duration, so it'd just be a sort of awkward addon that only helps in edge cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T21:09:27-08:00","id":804991,"title":"","content":"Alright, tweaked it.<br /> <br /> On another note, the idea for the following merit came to mind while watching Grimm:<br /> <br /> <b>Secondhand Sixth Sense (**)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Occult 2+, Empathy 2+<br /> <b>Effect: </b>While you can't sense it directly yourself, you've got a knack for noticing the slight look of surprise, the goosebumps out of nowhere, or the wide eyed look connected to the realization made by someone with a sense for the supernatural (even if they don't realize what it is themselves). Whenever someone you can see's Unseen Sense, a similar 'sixth sense' (such as Peripheral Mage Sight), or a power capable of otherwise revealing supernatural effects or creatures, is used to positively notice the supernatural, you may roll Wits + Empathy to notice the small telltale signs of realization, confusion, or disturbance that so often accompany it. This may be contested by Composure + Subterfuge for the individual if they would try to conceal their reaction.<br /> On a success, you realize that individual has such a sense or power, and has indeed noticed something supernatural. An exceptional success likely allows you to figure out what triggered it if the target knows, whereas a dramatic failure likely means you're all the more certain of the mundane nature of the situation.<br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers:</b> The ability is Unseen Sense and the Spooked condition is applied because of it (+2), you know the target has the capability (+2, stacks), the ability is reflexive and entirely unexpected (+1), the ability was actively used (-2), the ability was used by someone experienced with it (-1, stacks).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Balance Notes: I originally had it at 1 dot, to be less than Unseen Sense, but then realized that this applies to ANY sort of unseen sense or other supernatural insight, so it's probably a bit better than 1 dot, even if it relies on others. However, I can't see it being more than 2 because 3 is Aura Reading which seems strictly better, especially with the prerequisites added in, and the need for someone who has the appropriate capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 01-10-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T00:34:45-08:00","id":805064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=804991#post804991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I originally had it at 1 dot, to be less than Unseen Sense, but then realized that this applies to ANY sort of unseen sense or other supernatural insight, so it's probably a bit better than 1 dot, even if it relies on others. However, I can't see it being more than 2 because 3 is Aura Reading which seems strictly better, especially with the prerequisites added in, and the need for someone who has the appropriate capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is especially handy for mundane humans who spend quite a lot of time with supernatural beings, or just other human beings who happen to have supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T06:33:28-08:00","id":810601,"title":"","content":"I liked very much the homebrews presented here, specially the Mystery of the Fallen.<br /> \u200bI'm using it on my chronicle as a Mystery that my Dragon is developing, but I made some changes to it.<br /> <br /> On the 4th level, instead of the Rote quality, the bonus is equal this Coil lvl.<br /> And my Dragon isn't a mage, he's a megalomaniac Ventrue who has found a some others supernatural beings and now is studying and testing some properties of their bloods.<br /> <br /> The objective he has in mind is making the Kindred the Lords of other creatures, understanding and surpassing their capabilities.<br /> <br /> Can you give me some advices on how i can make a level 5 Coil for this, based on the previous levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 01-17-2016, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T11:38:22-08:00","id":810710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=810601#post810601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked very much the homebrews presented here, specially the Mystery of the Fallen.<br /> \u200bI'm using it on my chronicle as a Mystery that my Dragon is developing, but I made some changes to it.<br /> <br /> On the 4th level, instead of the Rote quality, the bonus is equal this Coil lvl.<br /> And my Dragon isn't a mage, he's a megalomaniac Ventrue who has found a some others supernatural beings and now is studying and testing some properties of their bloods.<br /> <br /> The objective he has in mind is making the Kindred the Lords of other creatures, understanding and surpassing their capabilities.<br /> <br /> Can you give me some advices on how i can make a level 5 Coil for this, based on the previous levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, if you want to make it more understanding and surpassing supernaturals in general, instead of gaining the fluidity/power of mages specifically, you could make it so that when you create a devotion based on the capabilities of another supernatural, you gain the same sort of discount, and in addition allow you to use that devotion (or perhaps powers in general) in a clash of wills to 'dispel' other powers that do something similar, even if a clash of wills normally wouldn't be appropriate (for instance, if you gained a devotion that granted you something like spirit sight, you could use that to dispel someone else's spirit sight, even though it couldn't normally affect someone else like that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T21:14:13-08:00","id":822105,"title":"","content":"So, I was considering waiting until I had them done, but that could take a while, so I'll just go ahead and post the two things I'm working on right now:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e7YshOL8exLJMweN0ydxWTrQMZKhKpz7JsKeDfTvdO8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Mechanical Bloodline Updates:</a> I've realized it's sort of redundant providing fluff that's already mostly been covered by existing sources; most bloodlines just need you to update the discipline list (sometimes), the bloodline bane, and the bloodline gift. So, this is a project wherein I go through a crapton of bloodlines and update them all mechanically, without adding any extraneous fluff (past a sentence or two to describe the bloodline gift in some cases). So far I've done the 1e core book's bloodlines, and a few from Bloodlines The Hidden.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ENK5kxk4R3BtfLbt_MZ5PtoDJpUF1kAb_9xf7ipYHcY/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Kindred Necromancy:</a> This goes hand in hand with the above, but will also be a bit of its own thing. Essentially, instead of having ten different bloodline disciplines that do some sort of necromantic thing, there will be a new blood sorcery that anyone can use, that covers all sorts of necromancy, and then each bloodline will have easier access to it, will make better use of it, and may have other nifty effects in using it based on their bloodline. I'll be filling rituals in as I convert necromantic bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Feel free to offer suggestions for some of the mechanics that are pretty directly converted, if you have an idea for making something fit the more monstrous bent of 2nd edition. I've done what I can, but it's not always obvious how these devotions and other capabilities can be changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 02-03-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T19:53:34-08:00","id":822990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=822105#post822105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to offer suggestions for some of the mechanics that are pretty directly converted, if you have an idea for making something fit the more monstrous bent of 2nd edition. I've done what I can, but it's not always obvious how these devotions and other capabilities can be changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't given a look yet at Kindred Necromancy, but I'm liking your conversions for some of the Bloodlines you've done, so far. I especially like comparing your take on the Qedeshah with <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nQ4PFxa1UDQ0qO6cs8u1UEZjd7HBKBu2GLXhw8Bl6Jc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">my own</a>, seeing as we had similar ideas with our respective conversions. Of course, I went down a very different direction with Berith.<br /> <br /> Will be interested in seeing how you do the Bak-Ra and Usiri, too. Seeing as those are two 1E Bloodlines I have already tackled with a conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:02:58-08:00","id":822998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=822990#post822990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven't given a look yet at Kindred Necromancy, but I'm liking your conversions for some of the Bloodlines you've done, so far. I especially like comparing your take on the Qedeshah with <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nQ4PFxa1UDQ0qO6cs8u1UEZjd7HBKBu2GLXhw8Bl6Jc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">my own</a>, seeing as we had similar ideas with our respective conversions. Of course, I went down a very different direction with Berith.<br /> <br /> Will be interested in seeing how you do the Bak-Ra and Usiri, too. Seeing as those are two 1E Bloodlines I have already tackled with a conversion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admittedly haven't ready many other conversions of 1e bloodlines, though at first glance I can see some of the similarities between ours; you used devotions exclusive to them and I used rites as their gift, but a lot of the mechanics ended up working similarly. But yeah, I decided to utilize blood sympathy rules since they're so much more developed in 2e. Regardless, glad you liked it!<br /> <br /> I'll make sure to quote your post again when I do the mechanics for those bloodlines","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:13:00-08:00","id":823004,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I <i>did </i>initially put a blood sympathy element into Berith, in the sense that each stage of the blood bond also created a simulated form of blood sympathy.<br /> <br /> * First Stage Vinculum granted a blood sympathy of one four times removed.<br /> * Second Stage Vinculum upgrades the blood sympathy to thrice removed.<br /> * Third Stage Vinculum upgrades it further to twice removed.<br /> <br /> What do you think, though? Should I incorporate it (again) alongside the dice tricks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:35:50-08:00","id":823021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=823004#post823004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I <i>did </i>initially put a blood sympathy element into Berith, in the sense that each stage of the blood bond also created a simulated form of blood sympathy.<br /> <br /> * First Stage Vinculum granted a blood sympathy of one four times removed.<br /> * Second Stage Vinculum upgrades the blood sympathy to thrice removed.<br /> * Third Stage Vinculum upgrades it further to twice removed.<br /> <br /> What do you think, though? Should I incorporate it (again) alongside the dice tricks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that working. Blood Sympathy provides benefits in both directions, and it's not terribly potent on its own to begin with, so I don't see it unbalancing what you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:54:44-08:00","id":825698,"title":"","content":"I've updated my Mechanical Bloodline Updates with a few of my favorites from Ancient Bloodlines (I'll do more over time), and updated Kindred Necromancy with new rituals. I added a lot of Kindred Vodoun's to it in updated form, and a few for the Apollinaire's Carrefour, but not any of the ones that didn't seem to fit the Necromantic flavor; universal understanding and most of the simple bad luck ones, for instance, nor Carrefour's levels that affected mundane doorways. I also changed Gris Gris to create a fetter instead, relying on ghosts instead of spirits.<br /> <br /> As a note, I added my Tremere bloodline here too, but there's a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/823150-because-i-m-crazy-the-tremere-in-2e\">thread </a>for that elsewhere already. Still, going to mention here I added a couple extra merits to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T19:22:41-08:00","id":829981,"title":"","content":"Hey,do you happen to have/know the guide for making Horrors from the Chronicles of Darkness core book? I'm kind of interested in knowing the mechanics behind creating one so I can do my take on the Children of the Seventh Generation (aka Lucifuge hunters) as a minor template. Maybe even weaving in concepts from DtD's Stigmatics, the spoilers for 2E Proximi, and your Forbidden Lore stuff (specifically the Breaches)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T22:19:18-08:00","id":830047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=829981#post829981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,do you happen to have/know the guide for making Horrors from the Chronicles of Darkness core book? I'm kind of interested in knowing the mechanics behind creating one so I can do my take on the Children of the Seventh Generation (aka Lucifuge hunters) as a minor template. Maybe even weaving in concepts from DtD's Stigmatics, the spoilers for 2E Proximi, and your Forbidden Lore stuff (specifically the Breaches)</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally they have Potency, which is a power stat of its own, which decides the number of dots they get in attributes, skills, merits, and dread powers; dread powers are very much like what they had in hunter, just capabilities monsters can have, and are very mix and match to make the creature you need. Said dread powers would likely work well as forbidden lore, but otherwise there isn't any systems for experience costs or the like for them, since they're designed for NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T01:30:03-08:00","id":830094,"title":"","content":"I see.<br /> <br /> Regarding Potency, how high up does it go as a power stat? Five dots? Or is it 10? Also, how many Dread Powers can a Horror get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:18:55-08:00","id":830237,"title":"","content":"It goes up to 10, for a maximum of 8 dread powers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:23:19-08:00","id":830243,"title":"","content":"Noted. Thanks.<br /> <br /> So, it's safe for me to assume that a Horror has [Potency/2] + 3 Dread Powers, more or less?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:48:26-08:00","id":830485,"title":"","content":"Not quite. it goes 3/3/3/4/4/4/5/6/7/8","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:32:27-08:00","id":830633,"title":"","content":"Ahh.<br /> Noted.<br /> Thanks.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:51:57-07:00","id":846933,"title":"","content":"Added Elder Transmutations to the list. The original thread for that is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846804-a-take-on-elders\">Here</a> if you have any comments on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T13:15:57-07:00","id":857261,"title":"","content":"Just to mention, I've added a couple more bloodlines to my mechanical update document, updated a few Tremere devotions in the Tremere document, and I think I added an Elder Transmutation since the last time I mentioned any updates, can't remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T16:38:23-07:00","id":870752,"title":"","content":"Added Icarians to the Mechanical Bloodline Updates and also tweaked the Septemi so they need two merits instead of one to gain the full effects; realized that was somewhat overpowered.<br /> <br /> Lemme know what you all think of Constance, and if anyone has a better idea for the Icarian weakness, let me know. I pretty much just gave it a very direct conversion for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 04-21-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:54:53-07:00","id":881243,"title":"","content":"Updated Tremere with detailed mage rules available, and went ahead and updated the Children of the Thorns to 2nd edition, though will probably tweak it further once Changeling 2e comes out and we know if the rules for the Hedge change at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:38:51-07:00","id":881354,"title":"","content":"Skimmed through the Children of the Thorns write-up, and I am liking what I'm seeing so far.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That said, I definitely need to revisit my Glass Walkers Legacy when I have the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:52:43-07:00","id":885661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=881354#post881354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skimmed through the Children of the Thorns write-up, and I am liking what I'm seeing so far.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That said, I definitely need to revisit my Glass Walkers Legacy when I have the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it!<br /> <br /> That said, after reading some clarifications on Legacies, I've gone through and updated it so they don't have extraneous reach; I was under the false impression instant casting was 'free' for legacy attainments. I left the second attainment as is, though, since it's &quot;special&quot; and conditional, applying only in the Hedge, I think that balances it more or less being about as potent as a scene-long attainment. Obviously, the 4th level attainment is its own special 'about as powerful' sort of thing, so also didn't need any tweaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:17:21-07:00","id":906515,"title":"","content":"So I decided to go through and tweak the &quot;Elder&quot; template at the end of the Elder Transmutations document, to incorporate more of the Methuselah facts and myths release from a while back, and to make them a bit more comparable to 2e Archmages. I've also more blatantly called it a Methuselah template, whereas your less 'established' elders would just gain access to Transmutations alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:55:46-07:00","id":906809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=906515#post906515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I decided to go through and tweak the &quot;Elder&quot; template at the end of the Elder Transmutations document, to incorporate more of the <u>Methuselah facts and myths release from a while back</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind linking me to that tidbit, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:08:47-07:00","id":906893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=906809#post906809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind linking me to that tidbit, please?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://blog.fantasyheartbreaker.com/2010/08/18/requiem-for-methuselahs/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://blog.fantasyheartbreaker.com/2010/08/18/requiem-for-methuselahs/\" target=\"_blank\"> Your Page Title </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://blog.fantasyheartbreaker.com/2010/08/18/requiem-for-methuselahs/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://blog.fantasyheartbreaker.com/2010/08/18/requiem-for-methuselahs/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:08:24-07:00","id":934697,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lhjffPJHxl6vsjT2kvSjrPesDlDhKry4UQxA9T_7S4I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Fuck Off, Mages</a>-A set of powers for Vampires, Werewolves, and Beasts that work very explicitly against Mages, for the sake of granting better protection against Awakened Magic. It assumes default rules, and also avoids using any of my own homebrew (So no Sanguine Objects or Elder Transmutations included), meant to be a very simple way to plug in a few defenses against Mages in any chronicle where conflict with them is common. I love Mages, of course, but there's certainly a lack of ways for non-Awakened to protect against them.<br /> <br /> The name is based on how DaveB worded Rebuke the Vizier as a &quot;Fuck off, mages&quot; power, which I found amusing.<br /> <br /> I did my best to vary the abilities, rather than just making 10 different &quot;Clash of Wills vs Magic&quot; powers, but a couple of those slipped in there. As a note, there's no Werewolf Gift for it because Gift of the Void already has a bit of the &quot;Fuck off, mages&quot; vibe to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 07-20-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:02:32-07:00","id":934787,"title":"","content":"Nicely done on these powers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Especially the vampire ones and the <i>Shaman's Curse</i> Rite. They definitely give the other splats useful counters against Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T23:34:58-07:00","id":934936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/477337-falco-s-nwod-homebrew?p=934787#post934787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nicely done on these powers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Especially the vampire ones and the <i>Shaman's Curse</i> Rite. They definitely give the other splats useful counters against Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like them! I know powers like those are a very specific niche, but it's still something that many splats were lacking, so I figured why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T05:10:12-07:00","id":945408,"title":"","content":"Since things affecting Mages only are only useful in, well, one case, I present <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1spHfzSvCfm3rc_H3BewMrctg-yQKf4U8nl6PCp49OLw/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Fuck Off Mages 2: Fuck Everything!</a> It provides the same splats with more universal protection, though obviously many of these are higher level, affect only certain things, or are otherwise less effective than the powers affecting only Mages. I need to think of a Rite for Werewolves still, I think, but I can finish that later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:02:32-07:00","id":954634,"title":"","content":"I've come up with a couple crossover-oriented things, inspired by the Crossover Chronicles as I was.<br /> <br /> The first is the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vndCTfB38aLJEl-LFxz2RZKt_7Q-LyfocDk_EuaSQ5Q/edit#heading=h.x60lv15ol4wr\" target=\"_blank\">Exterrianites</a>, a Legacy of Mages that seek to bring their soul into a form more akin to a Beast's Horror, so they're less weakened by their humanity and able to ascend in their understanding of the universe more easily.<br /> <br /> The second is a remake of the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dEFQlMw5XqybzitmHn9pdB5jrAzGkRLPTKWMElHT3xw/edit#heading=h.1bi0o64n3h8c\" target=\"_blank\">Dead Wolves</a>, something I know has been done before, but that I wanted to give my own take on, fixing some of the oddities the original bloodline had and making them feel a bit more like what they're supposed to be; pack animals.<br /> <br /> Finally, another bloodline, wholly new, the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1SKWyxboDZSZfXri5-xpI_OGKsQK1tZ-6aD8YyKh_GDA/edit#heading=h.1bi0o64n3h8c\" target=\"_blank\">Keijukainen,</a> a bloodline I've briefly mentioned elsewhere for the Nosferatu, wherein those spurned by even vampiric society seek acceptance among some of the denizens of the hedge, and find themselves changed in the process.<br /> <br /> Let me know what you all think. The Exterrianites I'm a little worried about, I feel like I need to get their whole idea across a bit better, both in writing and in their attainments, but I'm unsure what else to do, so I'm open to suggestions. Also open to ideas for other Fae Tricks for the Keijukainen, and whatever other feedback anyone may have!<br /> <br /> I'm a little burnt out for now, but I do have some ideas for Werewolf lodges, including one that follows a Supernal Entity of the Primal Wilds instead of a typical totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:24:41-07:00","id":954651,"title":"","content":"They all look interesting. However, I can't access the Legacy, and for the Haunt Bloodline, how do you decide the Dots of Goblin Vow (Blood) in regards to Vow of Blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:32:37-07:00","id":954655,"title":"","content":"Urk, check again, thought the legacy had been shared, guess I missed one.<br /> <br /> And it's one dot; goblin vow is a dot per subject